# Pinned Ibex RTL revision for this repository.
#
#   repository : https://github.com/lowRISC/ibex
#   commit     : 8b8ee086aef72e0833b7f0493d9d33f1e4d3c8e2
#   submodule  : designs/ibex/ibex
#
# This commit is the value recorded in the gitlink, so `git submodule update
# --init` reproduces it exactly. This file exists so the pin is greppable and
# so the run manifest can assert that the checkout matches it without needing
# a git subprocess: flow/run.py reads it and compares against `git -C
# designs/ibex/ibex rev-parse HEAD`.
#
# Do not bump this casually. Every episode records design.rtl_commit, and a
# bump changes every metric the extractor reports -- which means every episode
# taken before the bump describes a different design from every one after it.
# A bump is a fork in the dataset, not a version upgrade.

8b8ee086aef72e0833b7f0493d9d33f1e4d3c8e2

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How the VERILOG_FILES list in config.yaml was derived
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Ibex's own synthesis flow (syn/) drives Yosys through TCL and relies on a
# FuseSoC-generated file list, which this repository does not use. The list in
# config.yaml was produced instead by resolving the transitive dependency
# closure of `ibex_top` over the checkout:
#
#   1. index every `module` / `package` / `interface` declaration in the tree,
#      skipping the directories that never contribute synthesis sources
#      (ci, doc, dv, examples, formal, lint, shared, sw, syn);
#   2. walk outward from `ibex_top`, following `import pkg::*`, `include "..."`
#      and whole-word references to other declared identifiers;
#   3. drop files that are only ever `include`d, and record their directories
#      as VERILOG_INCLUDE_DIRS instead;
#   4. drop modules that nothing instantiates -- a package that merely *names*
#      a module (prim_secded_pkg does) would otherwise drag in the whole
#      library;
#   5. order the survivors: packages first, then modules, `ibex_top` last.
#
# Two `include`d headers are reachable from synthesised code:
#   prim_assert.sv        (vendor/lowrisc_ip/ip/prim/rtl)      -- unconditional
#   dv_fcov_macros.svh    (vendor/lowrisc_ip/dv/sv/dv_utils)   -- unconditional
# formal_tb_frag.svh is included only behind `ifdef FORMAL and is
# intentionally left off the include path.
#
# The list is committed rather than generated at run time on purpose: a
# generated list is a moving target, and this repository is about
# reproducibility. If the submodule is bumped, re-derive it and diff.
